// An array as a value, kept methods: casts: `method int g() { for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { x += 1 } return fa }
// initial state A do x = g() go to A`. KIELER rejects it: returning ‘double *’ from a function with return type ‘int’
// makes integer from pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion].
scchart Main { input bool b input int i int a[2] = {4,7} int c[2] = {4,7} int m[2][2] = {{4,7},{8,1}} float fa[2] bool ba[2] output int x output float f output bool y method int g() { for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { x += 1 } return fa } initial state A do x = g() go to A }
